   "w": 400,
   "h": 250,
   "text": "Pressure lockout: turn START on. The pump runs and the cylinder pushes out; at the end its rod reaches the limit sensor, which opens the 3/2 valve. The pressure fills slowly through the first throttle check valve (meter-in) into the gauge. When the gauge goes over 80 bar the lever is locked out: the pump stops, the cylinder returns and the second throttle check valve (meter-out) lets the gauge drain slowly to 0 bar. Turn START off to reset the lock. Turn the knobs to change the speeds.",
   "color": "#ffd166",
   "by": "Collab Share example",
   "t": 1,
   "z": 2
